    "description": "The International Community School of Addis Ababa is inviting all qualified, experienced, and motivated candidates to apply for the position of Electrical Section Coordinator . Position Title: Electrical Section Coordinator Reports To: Facilities Management Head Required Number: 1 Job Grade & Contract: Grade 7/ Full-Time SALARY: As per ICS salary scale. JOB SUMMARY The Electrical Section Coordinator is under the supervision of the Facilities Management Head, the Electrical Section Coordinator provides technical leadership, supervisory oversight, and operational management across all electrical, electromechanical, and appliance infrastructure for the school compound, the school apartment building, and leased residences. The incumbent ensures the safe, uninterrupted, and code-compliant operation of power distribution networks, powerhouse and backup generation facilities, fire alarm systems, HVAC and mechanical ventilation systems, pump house and swimming pool control systems, underground submersible pump control systems, campus sound systems, and institutional and residential electrical appliances, kitchen appliances service and maintenance. By managing the electrical workshop, preparing technical specifications for ordering parts, tools, and equipment, supervising and mentoring a team of electricians and electromechanical technicians, enforcing preventive maintenance programs, and leading electrical projects from initial planning and expansion demand assessment through execution and monitoring, the Electrical Section Coordinator safeguards institutional assets and delivers reliable operational support across the school community. KEY DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES 1. Leadership, Workshop & Technical Procurement Oversight Team Supervision & Mentorship: Direct, supervise, schedule, and mentor electricians and electromechanical system technicians; receive and distribute work orders, monitor field execution, set clear performance targets, and conduct annual performance appraisals in line with school criteria. Technical Specifications, Procurement & Workshop Management: Prepare accurate technical specifications for ordering replacement parts, diagnostic tools, testing instruments, and electrical/electromechanical equipment; prepare Bills of Materials (BOMs), initiate purchase requisitions, manage daily electrical workshop operations, ensure tools and machines are safe and well-maintained, and verify the quality of vendor-supplied materials and appliances. SOPs, Safety & Emergency Preparedness: Establish and enforce Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs), lockout/tagout (LOTO) and personal protective equipment (PPE) protocols, and emergency response plans for power outages and critical system failures across all school and residential properties. 2. Electrical Infrastructure, Powerhouse & Fire Alarm Management Powerhouse & Backup Generation Management: Oversee powerhouse operations, transformers, switchgear, automatic transfer switches (ATS), Fuel Stock Management and standby/emergency generators across the school compound, school apartment building, and leased residences to guarantee continuous, load-balanced power availability and timely servicing. Power Distribution & Specialized Lighting Systems: Direct the assembly, installation, testing, preventive maintenance, and repair of main and sub-distribution boards, circuit protection devices, data and power cabling, socket outlets, and specialized lighting systems (classroom, playground, security perimeter, and stage/drama lighting) in strict compliance with electrical codes. Fire Alarm & Security Electrical Systems: Supervise routine inspections, functional testing, preventive maintenance, and rapid fault resolution for fire alarm control panels, smoke and heat detectors, notification appliances, and CCTV/security electrical interfaces across campus and residential facilities. 3. Electromechanical, HVAC, Pump House & Sound Systems HVAC & Mechanical Ventilation Systems: Oversee the operation, scheduled preventive maintenance, and troubleshooting of heating, ventilation, and air conditioning (HVAC) units as well as mechanical ventilation and exhaust installations across school buildings and residential apartments. Pump House, Submersible Pumps & Swimming Facility Control Systems: Manage the electrical and electromechanical operation, preventive maintenance, and repair of the pump house, underground submersible pumps and their control systems, water supply booster pumps, pump control panels and switches, and swimming pool control, circulation, filtration, and heating systems. Sound & Audio-Visual Systems: Supervise the maintenance, repair, and event setup readiness of campus public address (PA) systems, sound mixers, amplifiers, microphones, speakers, and auditorium/amphitheater audio-visual equipment. 4. Institutional & Residential Electrical Appliances Management School Cafeteria, Staff Canteen & Laundry Facilities: Direct the routine inspection, preventive maintenance, and timely repair of commercial electrical appliances and equipment across the school cafeteria, staff canteen, and laundry facilities, including heavy-duty washers, dryers, commercial stoves, ovens, food warmers, water heaters, and distillers. Residential Appliances & Household Equipment: Oversee the installation, troubleshooting, repair, and scheduled servicing of electrical appliances and equipment across the school apartment building and leased residences, including washers, dryers, stoves, refrigerators, dishwashers, and water heaters. 5. Project Management, Campus Expansion & Residential Make-Ready Expansion Electrical Demand & Engineering Design: Evaluate electrical load requirements, power capacity, and infrastructure needs for building renovations, facility upgrades, and campus expansion projects; design, draft, and interpret electrical schematics, single-line diagrams, and architectural blueprints to ensure conformance to building and safety codes. End-to-End Project Execution & Monitoring: Manage electrical and electromechanical projects from initial planning, technical specification, and cost estimation through installation, testing, commissioning, and post-completion performance monitoring. Contractor Quality Assurance & Residential Make-Ready: Inspect and verify the quality and code compliance of electrical works executed by external contractors; conduct comprehensive electrical and appliance inspections and inventory checks for leased residences and apartment make-ready turnovers, reporting work completion to departmental leadership and the Maintenance Help Desk.",
