    "datePosted": "2026-11-27T08:39:56.000Z",
    "description": "Mission Description The Ministry of Finance (MoF) of Ethiopia, through the Technical Assistance to Domestic Revenue Mobilisation (MRI) Project financed by AFD and implemented with technical support from Expertise France, is supporting reforms to strengthen domestic revenue mobilisation and tax policy success. Ethiopia has rationalised and adopted targeted tax incentives to attract investment in order to, stimulate exports, substitute imports, transfer technology, and create jobs. In order to make the incentive regime targeted and effective, gaps were identified as two broad categories: 1) governance and 2) policy gaps. Accordingly, the first phase of the reform was correcting the governance gap by centralising tax incentives under the Ministry of Finance. The second phase of the reform was the policy gap, which was implemented later. Such a two-phase reform implementation has improved the effectiveness of incentives. However, such reforms should be strengthened by strong, evidence- and data-based implementation and monetary and evaluation. With support from partners and research institutes, the Ministry of Finance has recently conducted evaluations of tax expenditures. While these provide a solid basis, they remain partial, as they do not fully cover all incentives, as they only cover border or import-related incentives, excluding domestic tax incentives such as tax holidays, etc., limiting the ability to produce comprehensive reports. Monitoring and administration of granted incentives remain insufficiently structured. Most processes at the Ministry of Revenue (MoR) are manual. At the Customs Commission, management is more effective, but reporting to the Ministry of Finance (MoF) is not automated, limiting visibility on revenue losses and compliance. Coverage at the regional level is also limited. Project or Context Description I. Objectives and desired results 1) General objective The objective of the assignment is to provide high-level international technical expertise to support the Government of Ethiopia in designing and implementing modern tax-incentive data collection, database and management tools, evaluation methodologies, and analytical frameworks consistent with international standards. 2) Specific objectives 1. Assess data requirements and availability; design data templates and establish database framework; 2. International benchmarking and gap analysis of Ethiopia’s tax incentive framework 3. Tax incentive forecasting and evaluation methodologies; 4. Tax expenditure report estimation and forecasting tools, models, and approaches; 5. Cost-benefit analysis models (including data requirement identification or assessment, design data collection template, and database framework establishment); 6. Performance monitoring frameworks; 7. Technical guidelines for effective implementation of Regulation No. 586/2026. 3) Anticipated results Expected results include an international benchmark and gap analysis; practical ex-ante and ex-post evaluation and cost-benefit methodologies; a tax-expenditure report, estimation and forecasting tools; an investment-impact assessment framework; a performance-monitoring framework with measurable KPIs; technical inputs to guidelines and procedures; and training materials that support sustainable use by Ethiopian institutions. II. Description of the assignment 1) Planned activities Working under the supervision of Expertise France and in close collaboration with the Ministry of Finance, the expert will be responsible for carrying out the following tasks: The expert will Review international experiences and good procedures in tax incentive management; Analyse tax incentive frameworks applied in comparable countries; Identify policy and governance gaps, risks and opportunities for strengthening Ethiopia’s tax incentive governance framework. A. Development of Tax Incentive Evaluation Framework The expert will support the design and development of analytical methodologies, including: Identify data requirements, assess data availability, design data template, establish database framework; Development of ex-ante tax incentive evaluation methodologies and models; Design of cost-benefit analysis frameworks for assessing incentive effectiveness; Development of tax expenditure report estimation and forecasting models and methodologies; Design and preparation of investment impact assessment models; D Development of analytical approaches to assess economic additionality, employment creation, investment contribution, export performance, technology transfer and regional development impacts (as part of the cost-benefit analysis). B. Tax Incentive Performance Monitoring Framework The expert will: Develop a performance monitoring framework for tax incentive beneficiaries; Design measurable Key Performance Indicators (KPIs); Develop performance agreement templates; Recommend quantitative and qualitative performance thresholds; Support mechanisms for periodic review and withdrawal of ineffective incentives. C. Technical Advisory Support The expert will provide technical advisory services, including: Advice on the implementation of Tax Incentive Regulation No. 586/2026; If necessary, review and provide technical comments on draft guidelines and operational procedures; Recommend measures to improve fiscal efficiency; Support model testing of evaluation methodologies; Review analytical outputs generated through tax incentive databases and monitoring systems; Provide recommendations for institutional strengthening. D. Capacity Building and Knowledge Transfer The expert will: Deliver specialised technical workshops for stakeholders in the ministries; Provide training to the tax policy department; Review analytical reports prepared by roll player institutions; Support knowledge transfer on international tax incentive management practices; Develop training materials and practical guidance documents. The expert will: Deliver specialised technical workshops for stakeholders in the ministries; Provide training to the tax policy department; Review analytical reports prepared by roll player institutions; Support knowledge transfer on international tax incentive management practices; Develop training materials and practical guidance documents. Expected Deliverables: The expert shall provide the following deliverables: Deliverable 1: International Benchmark Report Including: Review of international tax incentive governance models; Qualified analysis; Lessons applicable to Ethiopia. Deliverable 2: Tax Incentive Framework Gap Analysis Report Including: Assessment of current Ethiopian practices; institutional and policy gaps; recommendations for improvement. Deliverable 3: Tax Incentive Evaluation Framework, including: Ex-ante and ex-post evaluation methodology; Cost-benefit analysis model; investment impact assessment framework. Deliverable 4: Tax Expenditure Estimation Methodology, including: Definition of methodology and format of the annual tax incentives report; Calculation approach; Data requirements: Reporting structure: A documented and reusable calculation template that the Tax Policy Department can operate independently without external support. Deliverable 5: Performance Monitoring Framework, including: KPI framework, ministries' monitoring approach, and performance agreement templates. Deliverable 6: Technical Review Reports Including: Review of draft guidelines; Review of database outputs; technical recommendations. Deliverable 7: Training Materials Including workshop presentations, technical guidance materials, and practical exercises. Deliverable 8: Final Technical Recommendations Report, Including: Consolidated recommendations, updated analytical tools, and a roadmap for sustainability.",
