    "description": "Organization: LEARN Logistics /by the Kühne Foundation – Ethiopia Office Duty Station: Addis Ababa or Jimma (depending on office assignment), with frequent travel across project areas in the Oromia Region Reports To: Country Director, LEARN Logistics Ethiopia About LEARN Logistics LEARN Logistics is a subsidiary of the Kühne Foundation, committed to building capacity in logistics and supply chain management (LSCM) across low- and middle-income countries. We focus on regions where public and private resources alone are insufficient to meet the growing demand for high-quality LSCM education that meets international standards. Our vision is a world without talent shortages in logistics and supply chain management, empowering global trade and fostering resilient economies. To achieve this, we invest in institutionalizing and strengthening local education systems, ensuring a steady pipeline of skilled graduates and professionals across university, vocational, and professional training levels for the logistics and supply chain management sector. Job Title: Field Project Manager for Oromya Regional State 2.1 Role Summary The Field Project Manager will be based either in Addis Ababa or Jimma depending on the Office assignment. The position will provide technical input and support in the LEARN Logistics Ethiopia Office project areas in the Oromia Region to ensure the quality of program implementation. 2.2. Key responsibilities Implement project plans and monitor project activities to ensure compliance with program requirements at the field level. Coordinate with implementing partners, community-based organizations (CBOs), and relevant government departments within the project area. Establish and maintain effective partnerships and linkages with regional stakeholders to ensure the successful delivery of project objectives. Plan, organize, coordinate, and facilitate regional training programs, workshops, and related activities. Manage training activities, conduct regular field visits, and provide technical guidance and handholding support to community mobilizers and district/block-level project teams as required. Oversee project management functions in the region, including planning, budgeting, implementation, and monitoring of LEARN projects. Facilitate project review meetings and ensure timely reporting, documentation, and dissemination of lessons learned. Coordinate closely with regional authorities and the LEARN Ethiopia team to ensure smooth project implementation and the provision of necessary technical and advisory support. Compile, consolidate, and submit timely and accurate progress reports on project activities and achievements. Monitor project performance against approved work plans, budgets, and targets, and recommend corrective actions when necessary. Ensure proper utilization and accountability of project resources in accordance with organizational policies and donor requirements. Perform any other duties and responsibilities assigned by the Country Director.",
