    "description": "About ZOA ZOA works with committed and motivated staff in serving millions of people affected by poverty, disaster, injustice, and conflict. Through the efforts of our dedicated staff, we are able to bring Signs of Hope and to support people who suffer due to armed conflict or natural disasters by helping them to rebuild their livelihoods. We value our employees and offer a wide range of benefits to meet the specific needs of our staff and their families. Purpose: The Country Human Resources Manager leads HR operations and people strategy, ensuring HR programs are delivered effectively and efficiently. The role coaches and mentors staff to identify strengths and development needs, champions gender equity, diversity and inclusion, and strengthens HR business partnering. The manager oversees security, represents ZOA externally, and builds its reputation as an employer. The role also advises country office teams and individuals, shapes strategic priorities, and helps solve operational problems to support a thriving global virtual team. Activities: Tasks, responsibilities, results: Strategy Implement the HR strategy and oversee recruitment, employee relations, workforce administration, engagement, payroll, and reward and recognition. Assess organizational needs and improve HR systems, policies, and practices to support ZOA’s work and meet its obligations. Develop HR metrics to guide decisions. Partner with the Country Management Team (CMT) to forecast staffing needs, plan for new roles, restructuring, and succession, and recommend priorities for organizational development and talent management. Improve staff engagement, welfare, and productivity by delegating HR responsibilities to line managers and developing their leadership skills. Manage the HR budget, monitor spending, apply financial controls, and approve expenditure within budget and policy. Lead and mentor the HR team, share leadership responsibilities, and strengthen project management, prioritization, and work planning to deliver HR commitments on time. Communicate HR priorities to internal and external stakeholders, coordinate across ZOA, and support project teams as needed. Lead staff relations and communications, including all-staff updates. Develop and implement HR initiatives that strengthen organizational sustainability and resilience, including helping plan staff retreats and leading selected sessions. Help enforce ZOA’s security handbook and local security plans Reward Lead remuneration policy and advise senior management on salaries and benefits using external benchmarks. Oversee HR administration and benefits, support Finance with payroll, manage broker and insurer relationships, respond to staff queries, and recommend new benefits. Monitor recruitment, staff development, and benefits budgets. Recruitment, Onboarding, Offboarding and Succession Planning Advise on employment policies and translate workforce plans into recruitment strategies. Lead hiring from job descriptions to offers, and strengthen the internship program as a recruitment channel. Partner with the Country Management Team (CMT) to standardize onboarding and orientation. Oversee offboarding, conduct exit interviews, and use findings to recommend improvements to the CMT. Work with the CMT to maintain leadership succession plans and develop promotion pathways and procedures. Develop the HR team’s skills, promote good practice, and uphold professional standards. Equip line managers to handle workforce issues and access HR guidance. Coach and mentor senior and high-potential staff to identify strengths and development needs, build effective working relationships, and support retention. Culture Strengthen a culture that reflects ZOA’s values and implement a gender, diversity, and inclusion plan aligned with its strategy and commitments. Model and promote staff wellbeing and support reasonable accommodations where needed. Work with managers and staff to develop, communicate, and apply HR policies that strengthen staff relations. Resolve complex issues and conduct thorough, impartial investigations as needed. Build relationships across program and support teams to improve coordination and communication. Foster a culture of performance and development by regularly reviewing individual and team progress and recommending improvements. Compliance Ensure ZOA complies with Ethiopian employment law, data protection and health and safety requirements, COTER obligations, professional standards, and internal policies. Track regulatory changes, advise management on required actions, and update HR policies and systems to reduce legal risk. Guide and train staff as needed. Maintain relationships with legal counsel, security groups, and professional HR networks. HR Data and Technology Maintain and improve the HR information system (HRIS) and expand the use of technology to support program and statutory requirements. Analyze HR metrics, including staff turnover, and use the findings to advise the Country Management Team (CMT) on strategic decisions. HR Governance and Advisory Ensure HR decisions are fair, transparent, effective, and aligned with ZOA’s values. Resolve complex HR issues and work with the Country Director and CMT to identify and mitigate people risks. Act promptly on whistleblowing reports, grievances, conflicts, and other urgent matters in consultation with the Country Director and in line with policy. Advise staff and teams on HR matters. Coach managers on recruitment, performance management, staff relations, and supervisory responsibilities, and build HR knowledge across ZOA. Organizational Processes Lead HR coordination meetings, share relevant updates, and follow up on decisions. Keep the team’s work plan current and realistic, and ensure deliverables are clear, accurate, and on time. Participate in line manager training and apply what you learn. With support from the Country Director, help teams reflect on their work and document lessons learned. Help staff set annual performance and development goals, create learning and development plans, and provide regular, constructive feedback. Build a strong team through effective recruitment, onboarding, performance reviews, and career development. Work with the Country Management Team and line managers to resolve HR and legal issues and support ZOA’s humanitarian objectives. Oversee HR work planning, monitoring, and evaluation, and lead coordination meetings that encourage participation and lead to clear actions.",
